ess">Sales / Business</option><option value="other">Other professional discipline</option></select><label>Owner briefing / positions Adam may rely on</label><textarea id="ownerBriefing" style="min-height:120px" placeholder="Example: Mechanical shop drawings are targeted for Tuesday. Do not accept any variation or cost. Ask the contractor to submit supporting documents for owner review."></textarea><label>Authority profile</label><textarea id="authorityProfile" style="min-height:90px">Answer technical and factual questions; ask for clarification; take notes; record requests for Mohamad. Do not approve variations, costs, contractual changes, purchases, payments, commitments, or date changes without separate owner approval.</textarea><div class="check" id="representativeApprovalRow" style="display:none"><input id="representativeApproved" type="checkbox"><label for="representativeApproved" style="margin:0">Owner representative session approval (synchronized with the main approval above)</label></div><p><b>Test operation:</b> use a second device/person as the meeting participant. Ask questions aloud or type them below. Adam should answer, speak, take notes, and refuse consequential commitments.</p></div><hr><b>Interactive Meeting Conversation</b><p>Approve once for this meeting session. Adam can then answer questions addressed to “Adam” and continue follow-up discussion. External actions and commitments still require their normal separate approvals. Do not promise, send, approve, purchase, trade, schedule, or execute external actions without the normal separate owner approval.</p>
